#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:87
#, no-c-format
msgid "Introduction"
msgstr "Introduccion"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:89
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&appname; is a &kde; Mail Checker that has the capabilities to dock itself "
"to &kicker;. &appname; can check the following types of mailboxes:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:94
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"mbox type (<abbrev>i.e.</abbrev>:<filename>/var/spool/mail/root</filename>)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:96
#, no-c-format
msgid "qmail"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:97
#, no-c-format
msgid "POP3"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:98
#, no-c-format
msgid "Imap4"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:99
#, no-c-format
msgid "nntp"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:100
#, no-c-format
msgid "and the ability to check on a process"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:103
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&appname;, checks your mail on an interval that is user specified for each "
"separate account. Once mail is received you can have &appname; run a 3rd "
"party program of your wishes or change the color/icon of &appname; while "
"docked in &kicker;. In addition to this you can have &appname; run a program "
"once you click on the docked icon in &kicker;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:109
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The rest of this chapter relies on the user to &RMB; click on the &appname; "
"icon in the &kicker; panel to access the appropriate menus."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:114
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Preferences Dialog"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:118
#, no-c-format
msgid "The buttons"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:120
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Preferences</guilabel> window is the most powerful part of "
"&appname;. At a first glimpse you may underestimate its capabilities, but "
"further under-the-hood you will find many ways to use &appname;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:124
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The first tab lists your current mailboxes. As default &appname; installs "
"<quote>Inbox</quote> as the default mailbox. The default <quote>Inbox</"
"quote> may not fit most users needs. With this default mailbox in place "
"&appname; will check the path <filename class=\"directory\">/var/spool/mail/"
"<replaceable>user</replaceable></filename> for new mail."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:131
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <link linkend=\"the-new-dialog\"><guibutton>New...</guibutton></link> "
"button will be covered in the next section. Please jump ahead if that is the "
"section you need assistance with."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:135
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you would like to remove the selected mailbox, click the "
"<guibutton>Remove</guibutton> button on the right. You can also copy the "
"selected mailbox if you don't wish to create two similar mailboxes twice."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:139
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Finally, after you have created a mailbox (see the next section), you can "
"modify it by selecting the mailbox you wish to edit and then clicking "
"<guibutton>Modify...</guibutton>. This dialog contains the same options as "
"when you click <guibutton>New...</guibutton>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:148
#, no-c-format
msgid "The <guilabel>Display</guilabel> Tab"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:150
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The display tab contains the options to change where &appname; will show "
"itself."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:153
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The first option, <guilabel>Horizontal</guilabel>, will create a window and "
"the contents of the window will contain the options you specified in the "
"<guilabel>View</guilabel> tab (which you can get to by selecting your "
"mailbox and clicking <guimenuitem>Modify...</guimenuitem>). On the other "
"hand, selecting <guilabel>Docked</guilabel> will dock &appname; into the "
"&kicker; panel."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:159
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The option <guilabel>Vertical</guilabel> is similar to <guilabel>Horizontal</"
"guilabel>, except the accounts stack vertically."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:165
#, no-c-format
msgid "The <guilabel>New...</guilabel> Dialog"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:167
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guibutton>New...</guibutton> button will load a window showing you what "
"mailboxes can be created for checking on a interval. Select your appropriate "
"mailbox type. If you don't know what type you should use, and you currently "
"use <application>&Netscape;</application> to check your mail, use POP3."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:173
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Following that window the modify options appear, allowing you to change all "
"aspects of the mail checking, including interval."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:176
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Each mailbox type (&ie;: Pop3, nntp, imap) has different server options, but "
"the rest of the options (including Poll, Commands, and View) are the same "
"(excluding mailbox type <quote>process</quote>). In these server options "
"dialogs you need to enter the appropriate information to fit your situation. "
"Keep in mind the default ports that are entered some of the server options "
"tabs are the normal ones used by the majority of the Internet."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:183
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The commands <guilabel>Poll</guilabel> tab contains one option that changes "
"the time interval between each check. Keep in mind this is in seconds, not "
"minutes."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:187
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Next, the <guilabel>view</guilabel> tab has options for changing the icon or "
"icon color while &appname; is docked in &kicker;. There are two options: "
"<guilabel>Use color</guilabel> or <guilabel>Use icon</guilabel>. Selecting "
"<guilabel>Use color</guilabel> will allow you to modify the colors. "
"Selecting <guilabel>Use icon</guilabel> will allow you to change which icon "
"is used for both <quote>Normal</quote> and <quote>New mail</quote>. Keep in "
"mind that &appname; can only use a icon or color, not both."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:195
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In the commands tab you can specify a command to be run once you receive new "
"mail in the <guilabel>New mail</guilabel> line. Also, the <guilabel>Click</"
"guilabel> line can contain a command to be run when you <mousebutton>left</"
"mousebutton> click on &appname;."
msgstr ""

